menu "Host link (PC / phone control protocol)"

    config HOST_LINK_IDLE_FLUSH_MS
        int "Idle gap after which undelimited binary data is forwarded to the radio (ms)"
        default 30
        help
            Data from the host that contains no line delimiter is forwarded
            to the radio after this many milliseconds of silence, but only if
            it contains non-printable bytes (a binary CAT protocol). Printable
            text keeps waiting for CR/LF so that typing in a terminal works.
            0 disables the idle flush.

endmenu
